  "_commit": {
    "id": "3781be6a974d746d3dc54021c3b4352a5418c37f",
    "author": "Damian <damian.szk@gmail.com>",
    "committer": "Damian <damian.szk@gmail.com>",
    "message": "Name experiments, not jobs, in values/ranks progress; version 2.25.6\n\nThe progress messages named STRING's job (\"STRING job bJKy...: running\"),\nwhich means nothing to the user. They now name the experiment:\n\n- One experiment: the values as typed, e.g. \"Experiment\n  example1_mapped$logFC: running (...)\" and \"...: 304 enriched terms.\";\n  a calculation is shown as \"values\".\n- A table: the submission names the experiments (the first 10, then\n  \"and N more\"), and each experiment gets a line when it finishes or\n  fails, with how many have finished. Experiments that STRING cannot\n  take yet are reported once.\n- get_values_ranks_results with job ids without names says \"Job <id>\".\n\nThe job id is still given when a job is submitted, and in the messages\nthat say how to get results later. Arguments and results are unchanged.\nThe quiet argument's help says what the messages name.\n",
    "time": 1794382728
  },
